{"repositoryId":1402938963,"availability":"available","full":"brynne8/pi-web-bun","name":"pi-web-bun","description":"Local browser UI for the pi coding agent, running on Bun with no Node.js toolchain","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-03T09:14:30Z","updated":"2026-10-15T14:59:19Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://agegr.github.io/pi-web/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:57.839Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:57.839Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:57.839Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T15:01:57.839Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is a Bun-focused fork of agegr/pi-web. It runs on Bun with no Node.js, npm or npx installed, and it has its own opinion about how a coding agent should read in a browser: a long command hands off instead of holding the turn open, a read call opens the exact slice it returned, the composer never changes what is under your finger, and a relay dropping its HTTP/2 stream no longer costs you the run. Differences from upstream says what still differs — and what upstream has since taken over; Bun setup gets it running. Everything else below is upstream's documentation.","Local browser UI for the pi coding agent. Pi Web uses the same local configuration and session files as pi, so you can browse and resume conversations, run agent turns, configure models and resources, and inspect project files from a browser.","Try the interactive demo → The real Pi Web UI runs entirely in your browser, with sample sessions, files and models. There is nothing to install; replies are pre-written and no model is called. That demo is upstream's build — this fork publishes none, so it will not show the differences listed below."],"features":["Session workspace: browse, resume, rename, export, and delete conversations grouped by project, with running state, context usage, cost, and compaction details.","Two ways to branch: New session creates an independent session file from an earlier message; Edit from here creates a branch inside the current session.","Background bash tasks (off by default): a long-running or over-long-output command hands off to a background task and comes back as a settled card instead of holding the turn open.","Background results that cannot be missed: settled reports arrive as one batch that wakes the agent once, each keeping its own card, and it can ask pendingnotifications what is waiting.","Project file tools: browse and upload files, inspect Git diffs, and preview source, Markdown, images, audio, PDFs, and DOCX files with automatic refresh."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brynne8/pi-web-bun/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"38712eb028d633f5a8f7f166d9656725c33f6082aa54d29134e3766df907cd5b","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:58.045Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:58.045Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This is a Bun-focused fork of agegr/pi-web. It runs on Bun with no Node.js, npm or npx installed, and it has its own opinion about how a coding agent should read in a browser: a long command hands off instead of holding the turn open, a read call opens the exact slice it returned, the composer never changes what is under your finger, and a relay dropping its HTTP/2 stream no longer costs you the run. Differences from upstream says what still differs — and what upstream has since taken over; Bun setup gets it running. Everything else below is upstream's documentation.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brynne8/pi-web-bun/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Web-based configuration: manage provider login and API keys, models, model tests, plugin packages, and skills without leaving Pi Web.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brynne8/pi-web-bun/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Web-based configuration: manage provider login and API keys, models, model tests, plugin packages, and skills without leaving Pi Web.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brynne8/pi-web-bun/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"If no model provider is configured yet, open the Models panel to sign in or add an API key. /.pi/agent is created on first use.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brynne8/pi-web-bun/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"If no model provider is configured yet, open the Models panel to sign in or add an API key. /.pi/agent is created on first use.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brynne8/pi-web-bun/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"38712eb028d633f5a8f7f166d9656725c33f6082aa54d29134e3766df907cd5b","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brynne8/pi-web-bun/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:58.046Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-15T14:59:19Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/brynne8/pi-web-bun/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T15:01:58.047Z","hash":"38712eb028d633f5a8f7f166d9656725c33f6082aa54d29134e3766df907cd5b","originalBytes":31638,"storedBytes":31638,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["bun","upstream","web","run","file","docs","one","what","session","pi-web","npm","browser","own","agents","test","agent","fork","tool","files","name","read","install","server","bash","dev","model","opens","card","path","proxy","instead","node","note","only","background","command","does","keeps","nothing","reads","row","build","call","open","project","running","still","version","arguments","each","git","markdown","node.js","off","panel","them","under","after","agegr","both","default","http","json","line","shell","shows","source","turn","two","because","before","commands","context","every","lib","npx","same","stop","subagent","text","view","where","which","while","code","exact","hostname","menu","next","per","port","profile","runs","sessions"